# Cloud Concepts Reflection

When I use my phone every day, I do not really think about how the apps work or where the information is stored. 
I just open them whenever I want to watch videos, listen to something, or talk to someone. 
After learning about cloud computing, I realized that many of the apps I use every day depend on cloud technology. 
The three services I use often are Netflix, Messenger, and TikTok.

* **Netflix** – I use Netflix to watch movies and shows during my free time. 
The videos are stored online, so I can watch them using my phone, computer, or other devices. 
I consider Netflix as **SaaS (Software as a Service)** because I use the application 
through the internet without managing the servers or systems behind it. 
It is also a **Public Cloud** because many people can use the same service.

* **Messenger** – I use Messenger to communicate with my friends and family. 
I can send messages, pictures, videos, and files through the internet. 
I consider Messenger as **SaaS** because I use the application without 
having to manage the computer systems that make it work. 
It is also a **Public Cloud** because it is available to many users.

* **TikTok** – I use TikTok to watch and share short videos. 
The videos and other information are stored using cloud services, 
which allows me to access them through the app. I consider TikTok as **SaaS** 
because it is an application that I use through the internet. 
It also uses a **Public Cloud** because many people can use the service.

Git and GitHub are important when working with cloud projects. 
Version control helps keep track of changes made to files and code. 
If someone makes a mistake, the team can look at older versions and fix the problem. 
GitHub also helps team members work together, share their changes, and keep the project organized. 
This can help prevent people from accidentally losing important work.

After learning about cloud computing, 
I understand that I use cloud services almost every day without noticing it. 
I also learned that Git and GitHub can make cloud projects easier to manage, 
especially when many people are working on the same project.
